# Avenue Properties — working rules

A marketing site for a real estate consultancy in Sector 75, Noida.

**Two phases. Know which one you are in.**

- **Phase 1 — the repo as it stands today.** A static site: no build step, no
  framework, no `package.json`. Open `index.html` and it runs. While there is no
  `package.json` in this repo, do not introduce React, Vite, Tailwind, npm or a
  bundler. Everything below describes this phase.
- **Phase 2 — the Next.js rebuild**, once `/app-next` exists. Stack, reasoning
  and the data model are in **`STACK.md`**; the task prompts are in
  `CURSOR-PROMPT.md` sections 9–16. Short version: Next.js 15 App Router +
  TypeScript, PostgreSQL via Supabase, Prisma, Vercel. The public site keeps
  this CSS as-is; Tailwind and shadcn/ui are used **only** under `/admin`.

The hard rules below apply in both phases. The design system, the copy voice,
the responsive contract and the evidence discipline carry over unchanged — only
the rendering layer changes.

## File map

```
index.html        home
buy.html          property for sale      } all three share one engine:
rent.html         property for rent      } Avenue.listing() in avenue.js
commercial.html   commercial + fit-out   }
property.html     detail page, read as property.html?id=<slug>
interiors.html    interior services
about.html        about, services, testimonial carousel
contact.html      map, enquiry form, list-your-property form
setup.html        INTERNAL console (noindex) — connect/test alerts + Google reviews

assets/css/avenue.css   the entire design system, 24 numbered sections
assets/js/config.js     the ONLY file to edit to go live (credentials, business info)
assets/js/data.js       demo inventory, localities, testimonials
assets/js/avenue.js     all behaviour, organised as Avenue.<module>
```

Every page loads the three scripts in this order, at the end of `<body>`:
`config.js` → `data.js` → `avenue.js`. Never change that order — `avenue.js`
reads `window.AVENUE_CONFIG` and `window.AVENUE_DATA` at definition time.

## The JS module map (`assets/js/avenue.js`)

| Module | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| `Avenue.util` | `$`, `$$`, `el`, `esc`, `params`, `store`, `put`, `waLink`, `telLink`, `mapsLink` |
| `hydrate()` | Fills every `[data-av="..."]` node from config — phone, address, hours, WhatsApp, maps, year |
| `header()` | Sticky header, drawer, active-nav matching by filename |
| `reveal()` | IntersectionObserver scroll-in, with a 2.6s safety net that force-shows everything |
| `shortlist` | Saved properties in `localStorage` |
| `searchConsole()` | Hero tabs rewrite the fields and route to the right page with query params |
| `Avenue.cards` | `.card(p)` and `.row(p)` — the only two places property card markup exists |
| `listing()` | Filters, sort, grid/list, pagination. Reads `data-purpose` / `data-segment` off `#listingRoot` |
| `detail()` | Renders `property.html` from `?id=` |
| `carousel()` | Testimonials |
| `Avenue.forms` | Validation + submit → `Avenue.alerts` |
| `Avenue.alerts` | Visitor + enquiry alerts, fanned out to every configured channel |
| `Avenue.reviews` | Google Business reviews, with a sample fallback |

## Hard rules

**1. Never hardcode contact details in HTML.** Phone, address, hours, WhatsApp
and map links all come from `config.js` through `data-av` attributes. If you need
a new one, add a case to `hydrate()`.

**2. Never write a colour literal in a component rule.** Every colour is a token
on `:root` in `avenue.css` (`--red`, `--ink`, `--muted`, `--line`, `--tint`…).
Changing the brand colour must stay a one-line edit.

**3. Property card markup lives in exactly one place** — `Avenue.cards`. Do not
hand-write a card in a page. If a page needs cards, give it a container and
render into it.

**4. The responsive contract.** The page body must never scroll sideways at any
width from 360px to 1440px. Before claiming a layout change is done, check:

```js
document.documentElement.scrollWidth - document.documentElement.clientWidth  // must be 0
```

Breakpoints already in use — reuse them, do not invent new ones:
`1180` (nav tightens) · `1080` (nav → drawer) · `1024` (utility strip hides,
listing filters move above results) · `860` (grids → 2 col) · `680` (→ 1 col,
call FAB appears) · `520` (search console stacks, forms → 1 col) · `390` (CTA
label shortens).

Any grid child holding text needs `min-width: 0`, and any `grid-template-columns`
using `1fr` should be `minmax(0, 1fr)` — both overflow bugs already found here
came from exactly that.

**5. Evidence discipline — this is a real business.** Never invent a statistic,
a RERA number, a certification, a client name, an award, a transaction count or
a "verified listing" claim. Everything in `data.js` carries `demo: true` and
renders a "Sample listing" badge, which `config.demoMode` controls. If you add
content that is not sourced from the client, label it as sample.

**6. Secrets.** `config.js` ships to the browser. Nothing belongs in it that
cannot be public. The Telegram bot token is the one grey area — it is visible in
page source, which is documented in README.md along with the Cloudflare Worker
relay that avoids it. Never put a Google API key in without a referrer
restriction, and never commit a real key to this repo.

**7. Accessibility is not optional.** Keep the visible focus ring, keep ARIA on
the tabs/drawer/filters, keep `prefers-reduced-motion` honoured, keep real
`<label>`s. Interactive things are `<button>` or `<a>`, never a clickable `<div>`.

## Conventions

- Vanilla ES5-flavoured JS: `var`, `function`, no optional chaining, no JSX.
  It runs with no transpiler, so keep it conservative.
- Escape every interpolated string with `esc()` when building HTML.
- Indian formatting throughout: `₹1.65 Cr`, `₹85 Lakh`, `1,595 sq.ft.`, `3 BHK`,
  `200 sq.yd.`, phone as `+91 70119 66691`.
- Copy voice: plain, specific, no marketing inflation. Short sentences. Say what
  actually happens. No "seamless", "unparalleled", "one-stop solution".
- Images are Unsplash placeholders. Keep the `?auto=format&fit=crop&w=…&q=…`
  query shape so sizes stay sane.

## Verify before saying it works

There is no test suite. The verification is the browser:

```bash
python -m http.server 4173     # then open http://127.0.0.1:4173
```

Check the console is clean, check the overflow number above at 360px and
1440px, and click the thing you changed. Do not claim a fix without doing this.
